<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spargapeithes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Spargapeithes was a king of the Agathyrsi, a people living in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, in the 5th century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> reports that he treacherously killed the Scythian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariapeithes">Ariapeithes</a>. He is one of the very few named rulers of the Agathyrsi, whom Herodotus describes as a people fond of luxury who wore much gold.</p></div>
